### Architecture and Control Logic Explanation                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
1. Tunable Parameters (PARAMS dict):                                                                                    
   All configurable values are consolidated into PARAMS (src/torcs_v3_physics.py:13) at the top of the file with clear  
   documentation:                                                                                                       
    - V_MAX (230.0 km/h): Maximum straight-line speed target.                                                           
    - V_CORNER_SHARP (70.0 km/h) & V_CORNER_FAST (140.0 km/h): Corner entry speeds for 90° vs shallow turns.            
    - BRAKE_DECEL (9.0 $\text{m/s}^2$): Assumed deceleration under full braking.                                        
    - STRAIGHT_DIST (100.0 m): Distance threshold above which the road is treated as a straight.                        
    - STEER_AIM (1.0), STRAIGHT_STEER_AIM (0.25), CENTERING_GAIN (0.40), TRACK_MARGIN (0.70), EXTRA_CENTERING_GAIN      
      (1.20), STEER_LOCK (0.366 rad): Steering gains and track boundary safety constraints.                             
    - ABS_SLIP (10.0 km/h), TC_SLIP (2.0 rad/s), TC_GAIN (0.08), WHEEL_RADIUS (0.3179 m): Anti-lock braking and traction
      control thresholds.                                                                                               
    - GEAR_UP_RPM (7200), GEAR_DOWN_RPM (3200), GEAR_HOLD_TICKS (15 steps / ~0.3s): Transmission shift limits and       
      anti-hunting hysteresis.                                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
2. Enhancement 1 — Kinematic Braking Model (calculate_target_speed (src/torcs_v3_physics.py:58)):                       
    - Computes free forward distance $d = \max(\text{track}[8], \text{track}[9], \text{track}[10])$.                    
    - Finds the angle of the longest range sensor ray to estimate corner severity: sharpness $=                         
      \frac{|\theta_{\text{aim}}|}{90^\circ}$.                                                                          
    - Interpolates corner entry speed: $V_{\text{corner}} = V_{\text{fast}} - \text{sharpness} \times (V_{\text{fast}} -
      V_{\text{sharp}})$.                                                                                               
    - Calculates target speed using kinematic deceleration: $v_{\text{target}} = \min(V_{\text{max}},                   
      \sqrt{v_{\text{corner}}^2 + 2 \cdot a_{\text{brake}} \cdot d})$.                                                  
    - Bypasses braking calculation and commands $V_{\text{max}}$ when $d \ge \text{STRAIGHT_DIST}$.                     
                                                                                                                        
3. Enhancement 2 — Racing Line Steering (calculate_steering (src/torcs_v3_physics.py:84)):                              
    - Aims along the open-road angle: $\text{steer} = \frac{\text{STEER_AIM} \cdot \theta_{\text{aim_rad}} +            
      \text{angle} - \text{centering}}{\text{STEER_LOCK}}$, clipped to $[-1, 1]$.                                       
    - Reduces STEER_AIM on straights ($d \ge \text{STRAIGHT_DIST}$) to prevent high-speed weaving.                      
    - Adds progressive centering when $|\text{trackPos}| > \text{TRACK_MARGIN}$ to keep the vehicle strictly on tarmac. 
                                                                                                                        
4. Enhancement 3 — ABS, Traction Control, Smooth Throttle & Transmission (calculate_throttle_and_brake                  
   (src/torcs_v3_physics.py:111), shift_gears (src/torcs_v3_physics.py:155)):                                           
    - Throttle: Full throttle when $> 10\text{ km/h}$ under target; proportional modulation when within $10\text{       
      km/h}$; throttle cut when braking or turning hard at high speeds ($> 50\text{ km/h}$).                            
    - ABS: Compares wheel linear speed ($\overline{\omega} \cdot r \cdot 3.6$) against car speed $v_x$; reduces brake   
      pressure proportionally if slip exceeds ABS_SLIP.                                                                 
    - Traction Control: Measures differential speed between rear drive wheels and front wheels ($\omega_{\text{rear}} - 
      \omega_{\text{front}}$); reduces throttle proportionally when exceeding TC_SLIP.                                  
    - Gears: Shifts up at GEAR_UP_RPM and down at GEAR_DOWN_RPM with a minimum hold time of GEAR_HOLD_TICKS simulation  
      steps.                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                        
5. Recovery Manoeuvre & Standalone Runner:                                                                              
